WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.736
The live Week 15 Moodle activity is labelled Course 9A: MCI, but its Preview SCORM opens a different internal title: Transport Logistics and Flight Physiology for Primary Care Paramedics. The internal body contains five teaching lessons and a glossary.
当前第15周Moodle活动标为Course 9A: MCI，但预览中的SCORM内部标题是“初级院前急救员转运物流与飞行生理”。该课件含五个教学单元和一份术语表。

00:00:17.736 --> 00:00:35.280
This course fills that verified Week 15 gap. It does not replace the separate MCI/START track, and it does not reproduce embedded knowledge checks. Current BCEHS helicopter procedures govern local field safety where generic course statements conflict.
本课补上经核实的第15周缺口，不替代独立的MCI/START课程，也不复制原模块内嵌的知识检查。若通用课件表述与本地操作冲突，现场安全以BCEHS现行直升机程序为准。

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:50.976
A moving ambulance, boat or aircraft changes what the crew can reach, see, hear and do. Transport planning therefore includes what care is feasible in motion, what must be addressed first, and how help will be summoned if the patient worsens.
救护车、船只或航空器移动后，会改变人员可接近、观察、听见和实施的内容。因此，转运计划应考虑途中能做什么、哪些事项须先处理，以及患者恶化时如何升级求助。

00:00:50.976 --> 00:01:05.424
Use the whole pathway: scene-to-vehicle, vehicle-to-destination, then handover. Reassess after major movement and whenever the patient, route, weather, resources or landing site changes.
要看完整流程：现场到车辆、车辆到目的地，再到交接。大幅移动后以及患者、路线、天气、资源或着陆点变化时，都要重新评估。

00:01:05.424 --> 00:01:24.576
Air transport can shorten a segment of the journey or reach a remote area, but the relevant comparison is time to appropriate definitive care—not flight time alone. Include activation, aircraft availability, weather, landing, patient transfer and onward ground travel.
航空转运可能缩短某段路程，或抵达偏远地区；但应比较的是到达合适确定性救治的总时间，而非单看飞行时长。要把调度、航空器可用性、天气、着陆、患者移交和后续地面转运都算进去。

00:01:24.576 --> 00:01:44.160
Use the school lesson’s four-T memory aid—time, terrain/traffic, treatment capability and team availability—to organize the discussion. It is a study aid, not an authorization rule; coordinate with dispatch, clinical oversight, the receiving service and flight crew as required.
可用学校课件的“四个T”记忆法整理讨论：时间、地形/交通、治疗能力和团队可用性。这只是学习辅助，不是授权规则；应按需与调度、临床支持、接收单位和飞行机组协同。

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:58.728
Ask what time is actually saved after the response and transfer sequence is counted. A helicopter may not be the quickest option for a nearby hospital, an unsafe site or a patient whose immediate needs cannot be met during flight.
把响应和交接流程全部计入后，再问实际节省了多少时间。若医院就在附近、着陆点不安全，或患者的即时需求无法在飞行中处理，直升机未必是最快或最合适的方案。

00:01:58.728 --> 00:02:10.752
Do not suspend immediate care merely to await a preferred mode. Reassess when the patient or weather changes and communicate the updated plan through the proper operational and clinical channels.
不能为了等待偏好的转运方式而停止必要的即时照护。患者或天气变化时应重新评估，并通过适当的操作与临床渠道通报计划调整。

00:02:10.752 --> 00:02:25.152
Before loading, identify which assessments and interventions may be needed en route. Place and secure equipment so that it does not snag, disconnect or block access; follow the device instructions and service procedure.
装载前先想清楚途中可能需要哪些评估和干预。设备应放置并固定到不会挂扯、脱落或挡住操作通路的位置；遵循器材说明和单位流程。

00:02:25.152 --> 00:02:42.144
Protect the patient from cold, heat, unnecessary exposure and avoidable movement. In rotary-wing operations, loose blankets, clothing, cables and bags can be lifted by downwash, so secure all items before the aircraft approaches.
避免患者受寒受热、无谓暴露或不必要移动。在旋翼作业中，松散的毯子、衣物、电缆和袋子可能被下洗气流卷起，因此航空器接近前要固定所有物品。

00:02:42.144 --> 00:02:54.912
Patient packaging does not prove stability. Continue the appropriate monitoring, compare trends, and reassess after stretcher loading, aircraft transfer, bumps or a clinical change.
完成固定并不代表患者稳定。仍要按要求持续监测、比较趋势，并在担架装载、航空器移交、颠簸或临床变化后复评。

00:02:54.912 --> 00:03:08.808
If an intervention cannot be done safely while moving, coordinate whether the vehicle should stop or the transport plan should change. Communicate early; do not let the desire to arrive quickly hide a deteriorating patient.
若某项干预在移动中无法安全完成，应协同判断是否停车处理或调整转运计划。尽早通报，不要因急于到达而忽略患者正在恶化。

00:03:08.808 --> 00:03:22.056
An ambulance is heavier and often taller than a passenger car. Its braking, acceleration and cornering response differ, especially when loaded or on wet, uneven or icy roads.
救护车通常比乘用车更重、更高。载重后或在湿滑、不平、结冰路面上，制动、加速和转弯表现都会不同。

00:03:22.056 --> 00:03:35.256
Smooth control protects the patient, the working partner and equipment. Lights and sirens do not remove road hazards or justify a speed that is unsafe for visibility, traction or traffic.
平稳操控可以保护患者、车厢内工作伙伴和设备。警灯警笛不会消除道路危险，也不能成为在视线、抓地力或交通条件不允许时超速的理由。

00:03:35.256 --> 00:03:48.360
The source lesson emphasizes vehicle readiness, road weather and defensive driving. Make the pre-trip check a real, locally defined checklist rather than an invented universal maintenance procedure.
学校课件强调车辆准备、天气和防御性驾驶。出车前检查应采用单位实际规定的清单，而不是自行编造一套所谓通用检修程序。

00:03:48.360 --> 00:04:04.512
A stable patient does not make an unsafe road safe. If visibility, traction, vehicle behaviour or another hazard becomes unacceptable, prioritize safe control, communicate the delay or stop and revisit the route with the appropriate team.
患者暂时稳定，并不会让危险道路变安全。若能见度、抓地力、车辆状态或其他危险不可接受，应先保证行车安全，通报延误或停车，并与团队重新评估路线。

00:04:04.512 --> 00:04:19.848
The BCEHS Spring 2026 procedure describes a Landing Zone Manager role for selection, hazard communication, readiness and perimeter control. The manager should not be simultaneously occupied with scene operations or patient care.
BCEHS《2026年春季》程序说明着陆区管理员负责选址、危险通报、就绪确认和周边管控。该人员不应同时被现场指挥或患者照护任务占用。

00:04:19.848 --> 00:04:33.144
Coordinate selection with Incident Command and relevant responders. The pilot-in-command has final authority over whether the site and approach are suitable; the flight crew may choose another location or decline to land.
选址应与事件指挥及相关救援单位协调。场地和进场是否合适，最终由机长决定；飞行机组也可以另选地点或拒绝着陆。

00:04:33.144 --> 00:04:53.472
The current public BCEHS Spring 2026 briefing defines the LZ as a safety zone plus the touchdown point. It gives a safety-zone guide of at least 40 paces by 40 paces, approximately 40 metres by 40 metres, and a preferred separation of at least 50 paces from the patient or accident area.
BCEHS现行《2026年春季》公开课件把着陆区分为安全区和触地点，并给出安全区至少40步×40步（约40米×40米）的参考尺寸；与患者或事故区宜至少相隔50步。

00:04:53.472 --> 00:05:12.480
The Moodle lesson also displays a generic 100-by-100-foot figure, then a different BCEHS dimension. Do not blend these into one rule: for BCEHS operations use its current 40-pace procedure and follow the responding aircraft’s requirements. The pilot retains final authority.
Moodle课件还出现通用的100×100英尺数字，随后又给出不同的BCEHS尺寸。不要把两者混成一条规则：BCEHS任务按当前40步程序准备，并遵循来机要求；最终决定权属于机长。

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:28.488
Walk and scan the whole safety zone when feasible. The BCEHS procedure recommends at least 50 metres between the LZ edge and power lines; if a site is closer, the hazard must be briefed to the pilot, and an alternative location may be safer.
条件允许时，步行检查并扫描整个安全区。BCEHS程序建议着陆区边缘与电线至少相距50米；若更近，必须向飞行员说明危险，也要考虑改用其他地点。

00:05:28.488 --> 00:05:42.072
Thin wires can be difficult to see from the air, particularly at night. Identify obstacles by direction and landmark, report them clearly, and never assume a light, cone or marker makes a wire safe.
细电线从空中尤其在夜间可能难以辨认。应以方位和地标清楚说明障碍物，不能认为灯光、锥桶或标记能让电线变安全。

00:05:42.072 --> 00:05:56.064
A landing zone is more than an empty patch of ground. The team needs a clear perimeter, a patient-transfer route and a shared understanding of who controls access, who communicates and what happens if conditions change.
着陆区不是一块空地就够了。团队还需要明确的周界、患者转运通道，并共同确认谁管控进出、谁负责通报，以及条件变化时如何行动。

00:05:56.064 --> 00:06:08.400
Do not use people as markers around the landing perimeter. People may control access from a safe position, while visible markers are used only as approved by the current procedure and flight crew.
不要让人员站在着陆区边缘充当标志。人员应在安全位置管控进入，标识物则必须按现行程序和机组要求使用。

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:23.136
Use the authorized channel and the local agency’s call format. Report the status plainly: ready, not ready, or how many minutes are needed. Give the LZ location and its relationship to the scene or a known landmark.
使用获准频道和本地单位呼号格式，清楚说明着陆区状态：已就绪、未就绪，或预计还需多久。并说明位置及其与事故现场或已知地标的关系。

00:06:23.136 --> 00:06:38.688
Include estimated wind direction and speed, visibility and every relevant obstacle. Update the report when conditions change. Do not direct the aircraft’s approach path; transmit observations and let the pilot decide.
报告估计风向、风速、能见度和所有相关障碍。条件变化时及时更新。不要替航空器指定进场路线；应报告观察结果，由机长决定。

00:06:38.688 --> 00:06:52.704
Night-vision equipment does not make darkness equivalent to daylight. Weather, dust, snow, rain, smoke, glare and narrow obstacles can reduce visibility even when crews use night-vision goggles.
夜视设备并不能把黑夜变成白天。天气、尘土、雪、雨、烟雾、眩光和细小障碍都可能降低能见度，即使机组使用夜视镜也是如此。

00:06:52.704 --> 00:07:08.616
BCEHS notes that some LED beacons may be invisible to night-vision goggles and that crews may request strobes be turned off. Use only approved lighting, never improvise aircraft-directed illumination, and follow the crew’s current instructions.
BCEHS指出，某些LED信标可能无法被夜视镜观察到，机组也可能要求关闭频闪灯。只能使用批准的照明方式，不要自行用灯照射航空器，并遵从机组当前指令。

00:07:08.616 --> 00:07:38.520
On final approach, the landing-zone manager clears outside the safety zone and watches for hazards, keeping radio traffic safety-critical. If a hazard appears, transmit: abort, abort, abort. The BCEHS visual alternative is to extend both arms overhead and wave them in a crossing motion. If in doubt, call the abort; remain in communication and explain the hazard. The pilot-in-command retains the landing decision.
最后进场时，着陆区负责人退到安全区外观察危险，无线电仅保留安全关键通信。发现危险时发出：ABORT，ABORT，ABORT。BCEHS规定的视觉替代信号是双臂举过头顶，交叉挥动。有疑虑时呼叫中止，保持联络并解释危险；最终降落决定仍由机长作出。

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:53.496
Do not clear an aircraft into an LZ that is not ready. If the aircraft overshoots or aborts, remain in communication and follow the agreed next step; do not restart the approach until the hazard and authorization are resolved.
着陆区尚未就绪时，不要报告可以降落。若航空器复飞或中止，应保持联络并遵循约定的下一步；危险尚未消除或授权尚未确认前，不要自行重新开始进场。

00:07:53.496 --> 00:08:12.336
Transport Canada advises following crew instructions and avoiding rotor hazards. The current BCEHS Spring 2026 LZ procedure is more specific for local scene operations: do not approach until the rotors have completely stopped and a pilot gets out and waves responders forward.
Transport Canada要求遵从机组指令并避开旋翼危险。BCEHS现行《2026年春季》着陆区程序对本地现场操作规定更具体：必须等旋翼完全停止、飞行员下机并招手示意后才可接近。

00:08:12.336 --> 00:08:28.440
The Moodle lesson’s generic “front or side while crouched” wording conflicts with that current BCEHS rule. Do not use it to approach an active aircraft. Aircraft type and operator procedures vary; the flight crew controls the authorized route.
Moodle课件中通用的“蹲低从前方或侧方接近”与BCEHS现行规定冲突。不得据此接近旋翼仍在运转的航空器。机型和运营方程序不同，获准路线由飞行机组决定。

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:47.256
Identify yourself as the primary ground caregiver and give the flight paramedic a short, structured report: what happened, what you found, what changed, what you did and the current vital-sign trend. Include identification or known allergies when available and appropriate.
向飞行医护人员说明自己是地面主要照护者，并提供简洁结构化报告：发生了什么、发现了什么、变化如何、已做了什么，以及当前生命体征趋势。可用时提供身份信息和已知过敏史。

00:08:47.256 --> 00:09:06.120
Follow the flight paramedic and pilot directions for loading and transfer. BCEHS says not to load equipment or operate aircraft doors unless asked. Keep the site clear after takeoff; its 2026 briefing says maintain the LZ for about five minutes in case the aircraft must return.
装载和移交时遵从飞行医护人员及飞行员指令。BCEHS规定，除非被要求，否则不要装载设备或操作航空器舱门。起飞后保持现场清空；其2026课件要求着陆区继续保持约五分钟，以防航空器需要返回。

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:19.320
During ascent, lower ambient pressure can expand a closed gas collection. The Week-15 school lesson emphasizes that this can matter for pneumothorax, other trapped gas and air-containing equipment.
上升时环境压力降低，封闭气体可能膨胀。学校第15周课程强调，这会影响气胸、其他滞留气体以及含气设备。

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:34.848
The size of the effect depends on actual cabin altitude, pressurization, flight profile and the patient or device. Do not assume every helicopter flight produces the same pressure change or make an intervention solely from the gas-law principle.
影响大小取决于实际舱压高度、加压情况、飞行剖面及患者或设备。不要假设每次直升机飞行都会产生相同压力变化，也不要仅凭气体定律就实施某项干预。

00:09:34.848 --> 00:09:48.576
Oxygen remains about 21 percent of dry air, but the total atmospheric pressure decreases with altitude. The result is a lower oxygen partial pressure, which can worsen hypoxia in a vulnerable patient.
干燥空气中的氧仍约占21%，但海拔升高时总气压下降，因此氧分压也降低，可能使脆弱患者的缺氧加重。

00:09:48.576 --> 00:10:05.352
Actual exposure varies with the aircraft, cabin pressure, route and operating altitude. Follow the current clinical protocol and flight-team plan for oxygen, monitoring and escalation; there is no universal altitude or saturation rule in this lesson.
实际影响取决于机型、舱压、路线和运行高度。氧疗、监测和升级处理应遵循现行临床规程及机组计划；本课不设通用的飞行高度或血氧阈值。

00:10:05.352 --> 00:10:17.880
A helicopter cabin can be noisy, vibratory and constrained. The course teaches these as operational stressors, not as proof that a particular measurement is always impossible.
直升机舱内可能噪声大、振动强且空间受限。学校课件把这些列为操作压力因素，但这不等于某项测量必然无法完成。

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:33.624
Before flight, confirm with the flight crew which equipment is available, where it can be secured and how communication will work. Do not rely on a monitor reading without considering motion, signal quality, device limits and the patient’s full presentation.
飞行前应与机组确认可用设备、固定位置及沟通方式。解读监护仪时要考虑运动、信号质量、设备限制和患者整体表现，不能只凭一个读数下结论。

00:10:33.624 --> 00:10:47.208
For a patient at risk from gas expansion or hypoxia, identify the concern before flight, communicate it to the flight crew and agree on monitoring, equipment and escalation under the approved protocol.
对存在气体膨胀或缺氧风险的患者，应在飞行前识别问题、通报机组，并按批准规程共同确认监测、设备和升级方案。

00:10:47.208 --> 00:11:03.000
The Moodle lesson mentions changing the volume of air-filled devices. This track does not direct you to deflate an endotracheal cuff or alter any device. Use the device instructions, scope, medical direction and flight-provider procedure.
Moodle课件提到调整含气设备体积。本课不指示放空气管导管套囊或更改任何设备；应遵循器材说明、执业范围、医疗指导和航空运营方程序。

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:20.136
In this original case, do not choose “air” merely because it is shorter on a map. Compare the whole time to appropriate care, the patient’s changing condition, weather, available crew, route and whether a secure landing and transfer can actually be completed.
在这个原创病例中，不要只因地图上的距离较短就选航空转运。要比较到达适当救治的总时间、患者变化、天气、机组可用性、路线，以及能否真正完成安全着陆和移交。

00:11:20.136 --> 00:11:36.960
If wind or rain makes the LZ unsafe, report the hazard and wait for a safe plan. Continue appropriate care while coordinating; once transfer is authorized, reassess after each major movement and hand over the patient’s status and trend.
若风雨使着陆区不安全，应报告危险并等待安全方案。协同期间继续适当照护；获得转运安排后，每次大幅移动后都要复评，并向机组交代患者状态和趋势。

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:49.896
If a number or approach rule differs between a generic module and the current BCEHS briefing, stop and resolve the discrepancy before practice. Do not blend sources into a third, invented procedure.
若通用模块与BCEHS现行课件中的数字或接近规则不同，练习前先暂停并解决差异。不要把不同来源拼成第三套自创程序。

00:11:49.896 --> 00:12:06.792
This narrated course prepares your reasoning; it does not certify driving, LZ management, aircraft approach, flight procedures or medical competency. Hands-on actions require the school instructor, current operator procedures and supervised practice.
本配音课程用于准备思路，不会认证驾驶、着陆区管理、航空器接近、飞行程序或医疗能力。实际操作必须遵循学校教师、运营方现行程序并接受监督训练。
